  "contextText": "Subject: Basic Electrical Engineering (EE101). Topic: Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL) and Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL). Recap of Ohm's law V = IR. Conservation of charge at a node/junction, conservation of energy around a closed loop, EMF and IR drops, sign conventions, power dissipated P = I^2 R, charge as the integral of current. Next class: mesh analysis.",
